    LOW gap with HIGH single-target movement.

  the split's OWN cost     `fixed+on` -0.7 -- an unconditional lesson on
                           a split table, which is its WORST case and not a
                           power measurement (it fell with more ticks)
  the tables diverged      0.0258 against a shared |bias| of 0.0163
  the creature was in ctx  100% of ticks
  dF1 on -- off            31.4 -> 51.5 Hz (lift +20.1, 1.1 SE)
  dF1 on -- random         19.6 -> 51.5 Hz (+31.9, 2.0 SE)
  against the oracle       21.8% of 236 Hz

  IT DOES NOT LEARN, AND THAT IS THE FIRMEST CLOSURE OF G3 ON FILE.
  The tables DID diverge (0.0258), so the estimator ran and wrote
  different things into the two contexts. The voice still does not
  depend on the word: 51.5 Hz against 31.4 with the mechanism off and
  19.6 against the matched-marginal control, where a perfect bias on this
  same readout reaches 236.

  Every earlier null here had a delivery excuse -- the condition did not
  arrive, the tract could not carry it, the readout could not express it.
  This one has none. `ctxbias` showed the bias route is free and the
  optimum is representable; v51 makes it representable IN THE CREATURE
  and the estimator does not find it. What is left is the estimator
  itself -- Gadagkar's performance prediction error rather than the raw,
  object-blind R this creature delivers.
